WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.080
Thin MXene sheets conduct electricity like a metal, which makes them promising for energy storage worn on the body.

2
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:16.200
To use it near the body, we need to know if it is safe. Data on MXene toxicity in living bodies were scarce and sometimes conflicting.

3
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:29.000
The team gave the same nanosheets to rats by three routes, skin, mouth and abdominal cavity, and checked blood and five organs. No major abnormalities appeared at the tested doses, with some mild changes.

4
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:39.800
A supercapacitor built from the same nanosheets stored 66.43 millifarads per square centimeter and kept 95 percent after five thousand cycles.

5
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:47.480
Bent at several angles, or worn on the back of a bending hand, its charge and discharge times barely changed.

6
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:55.320
One material, studied from energy storage to toxicity. A first step toward electronics worn on the body.
